            <ArticleTitle>[Leu-enkephalin levels in the blood of patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A total of 32 CHD patients with angina pectoris of effort, functional class I-IV, aged 46 to 68 were examined. Eight patients with cervical osteochondrosis of the same age were controls. In CHD patients with angina pectoris, functional class I-II, the content of leu-enkephalin in the blood plasma did not differ from that in the control group whereas in patients with angina pectoris, functional class II-IV, it was lowered by 42%. In CHD patients aged 46 to 55 the level of leu-enkephalin in the blood plasma was raised, in the group of patients aged 55 to 68 it was considerably lowered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
